=== stdout ===
OVERVIEW: List Firebase Crashlytics issues.

Results follow Firebase topIssues impact order, counted over --since (default
7d, at most 90d).
Bare issues fetches --limit issues. Queries and filters fetch a wider search
window by default,
then show the first --limit matches. --crash-directory implies --xcode; without
a configured
Firebase app, --xcode lists local crashes only.

USAGE: xcrashlytics issues [<options>] [<query>]

ARGUMENTS:
  <query>                 Optional title/subtitle/module/file/symbol query.

OPTIONS:
  --format <format>       Output format: text (default), json, or ndjson.
                          (values: text, json, ndjson; default: text)
  --limit <limit>         Limit displayed issues (and, separately, displayed
                          Xcode crashes). (default: 20)
  --search-limit <search-limit>
                          Number of Firebase issues to fetch before filtering
                          (at most 2000).
  --all                   Search up to 2000 Firebase issues before filtering.
  --match <match>         Case-insensitive substring filter for
                          title/subtitle/module/file/symbol.
  --type <type>           Filter by Firebase error type, for example FATAL,
                          NON_FATAL, EXC_BAD_ACCESS.
  --min-events <min-events>
                          Only include issues with at least N events.
  --app-version <app-version>
                          Only count events of this exact app version (6.16.0,
                          or 6.16.0 (937) for one build); issues and counts
                          cover only it.
  --since-version <since-version>
                          Only count events of app versions greater than or
                          equal to this one; issues and counts cover only them.
  --file <file>           Only include issues whose parsed top file exactly
                          matches this value.
  --symbol <symbol>       Only include issues whose parsed top symbol exactly
                          matches this value.
  --since <since>         Report window for event and user counts: 24h, 7d,
                          30m, 2w, or all (90d). Default 7d, at most 90d.
  --by-day                Include exact per-day event counts for displayed
                          issues (UTC days, from the report).
  --events-per-issue <events-per-issue>
                          Events to scan per issue for --user-id (default 50).
  --user-id <user-id>     Only include issues with a sampled event for this
                          exact Firebase user id.
  --domain <domain>       Only include issues whose latest event metadata
                          contains this NSError/domain string.
  --user-info-key <user-info-key>
                          Filter latest event userInfo by key or key=value.
                          Repeatable: --user-info-key a --user-info-key b.
  --xcode                 Include local crash reports downloaded by the Xcode
                          Organizer.
  --crash-directory <crash-directory>
                          Xcode crash directory to scan; implies --xcode.
                          Repeatable.
  --version               Show the version.
  -h, --help              Show help information.

